  <section|Treatment><label|treatment>

  Prove (elementary). No literature result is needed: the only facts used are
  <verbatim|log x \<less\>= x - 1>, monotonicity of <verbatim|exp> and of
  <verbatim|c -\<gtr\> M^c> for <verbatim|M \<gtr\>= 1>, and <verbatim|(log
  t)^48 / t -\<gtr\> 0>.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  All declarations were read textually; no Lean was elaborated.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  item>>|<cell|<strong|Declarations and paths>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|Clock,
  <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-clock-cap-rate>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Calendar.hatBeta>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/RG/History.lean>: <verbatim|bar + G.slopeConstant *
  schedule.scale m>); <verbatim|fits.delayed : 1 \<less\> hatBeta t> (used in
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.bell>, <verbatim|lira>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Lyre.lean>);
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.hrate> (same file, <verbatim|hatBeta -\<gtr\>
  infinity>, needs <verbatim|G.Simple>)>|<cell|<verbatim|kappa =
  slopeConstant \<gtr\> 0>. The text uses only <verbatim|hatBeta_j \<gtr\> 1>
  and <verbatim|hatBeta_j -\<gtr\> infinity>.>>|<row|<cell|Monitor
  <verbatim|M_j = exp((log log hatBeta_j)^2)>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Calendar.monitor>
  (<verbatim|History.lean>)>|<cell|Exact match. Same object as
  <verbatim|\\mathcal M_k> in <verbatim|allarity-marked-propagation.tex> l.
  250 and <verbatim|rank-root-normalization.tex>.>>|<row|<cell|Magnified
  monitor <verbatim|M_j^c>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Station.mag A b k :=
  A.clock.monitor k ^ b> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Station.lean>)>|<cell|Real
  power (<verbatim|rpow>); <verbatim|mag_pos>.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|def:ex-lattice-tiltcap>,
  <verbatim|tiltcap(j) = exp((log log hatBeta_j)^3)>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tilt_cap
  P i := Station.mag P (Perch.y (P.clock.hatBeta i)) i>
  (<verbatim|Terrace/Fund.lean>); <verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Perch.y s := log
  (log s)> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Reign.lean>)>|<cell|<verbatim|mag> at
  exponent <verbatim|y = log log hatBeta>. The closed form
  <verbatim|exp(u^3)> is the computation inside the proof of
  <verbatim|titles> (<verbatim|(exp (u^2))^u = exp(u^2 *
  u)>).>>|<row|<cell|Ticket>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Ticket P a v :=
  forall b \<gtr\> a, eventually 0 \<less\>= v i \<less\>= watch P b i>,
  <verbatim|watch P b k = exp (b * Gate (hatBeta k))>, <verbatim|Gate x =
  (log x)^48> (<verbatim|Fund.lean>, <verbatim|Terrace/Base.lean>)>|<cell|Exact
  match (nonnegativity eventually, as in the source).
  <verbatim|trace-small-means.tex> states the notion for nonnegative
  sequences; the two agree there.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|lem:ex-lattice-trace-tiltcap-ticket>
  (1), (2) for <verbatim|p = 1>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.titles :
  Ticket P 0 (tilt_cap P)> (<verbatim|Fund.lean>)>|<cell|Source proof:
  eventually <verbatim|log hatBeta \<gtr\>= 1> (<verbatim|lrate>), and
  <verbatim|u^3 \<less\>= (log hatBeta)^3 \<less\>= b (log hatBeta)^48> via
  <verbatim|gate_flex 3> (<verbatim|Terrace/Stanza.lean>). Same argument as
  the manuscript.>>|<row|<cell|Lemma (2), general <verbatim|p> (the fifth
  power used by small means)>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Ticket.pows>
  (<verbatim|Fund.lean>)>|<cell|Source derives powers by repeated
  <verbatim|Ticket.push>; the manuscript gives the direct bound <verbatim|p
  u^3 \<less\>= p L^3 \<less\>= rho' L^48> once <verbatim|L^45 \<gtr\>=
  p/rho'>. Reorganised, same conclusion.>>|<row|<cell|Chart receipt
  <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-clock-cap-receipt>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.East.TimberSky.high
  : 5 \<less\> b \<wedge\> b \<leq\> Perch.y (clim A i)>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Prom/Zoom/Boats.lean>), with
  <verbatim|Vane.checked V i := TimberSky F a d V.k i V.b V.c V.R>, so
  <verbatim|i := V.k> (frame level); <verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.clim A k :=
  A.clock.hatBeta k> (<verbatim|Next/RANK/ParticleGate.lean>);
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.b_zoom V i := mag A (V i).b (V i).k> and
  <verbatim|kamago : X.r i = a_{(V i).k} * b_zoom V i>
  (<verbatim|Terrace/SkyEar.lean>); <verbatim|Gondola.season>
  (<verbatim|Terrace/Gondola.lean>); <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tiltP>
  (<verbatim|Terrace/Cabin.lean>)>|<cell|Zoom factor <verbatim|b_i =
  M_{j_i}^{c_i}> with <verbatim|5 \<less\> c_i \<less\>= log log
  hatBeta_{j_i}>, for every <verbatim|i>. Upper bound is <verbatim|tiltP>;
  lower bound <verbatim|b_i \<gtr\>= 1> follows from <verbatim|M \<gtr\>= 1>,
  <verbatim|c_i \<gtr\> 0> (the source instead uses <verbatim|grow_big>,
  <verbatim|b_zoom -\<gtr\> infinity>, which needs only the tail).
  <verbatim|trace-firesky-gallery.tex> l. 39\U41 states <verbatim|5 \<less\>
  b> and "no larger than the permitted angular bound"; the value
  <verbatim|log log hatBeta> of that bound is read from
  <verbatim|TimberSky.high>.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|lem:ex-lattice-trace-log-zoom>,
  <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-trace-log-zoom>>|<cell|Inside
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.zoom_BQ> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Orr.lean>):
  <verbatim|f i \<leq\> tilt_cap P' (k i)> from <verbatim|tiltP> and
  <verbatim|(hq.season i).1.high.2>, then <verbatim|\<leq\> watch _ 1 (k i)>
  from <verbatim|titles P' h 1>; <verbatim|log f i / m i -\<gtr\> 0> by
  squeeze with <verbatim|Gate_calm> (<verbatim|Terrace/Lyre.lean>)>|<cell|Here
  <verbatim|k i = (V i).k> is the frame level <verbatim|j_i> and <verbatim|m
  i = hatBeta (k i)>. The source bound is <verbatim|log b_i \<less\>= (log
  hatBeta_{j_i})^48> (rate 1 ticket); the manuscript proves the stronger
  <verbatim|(log log hatBeta)^3>, which implies it. Lower bound in the
  source: <verbatim|grow_big> eventually <verbatim|\<gtr\>= 1>.>>>>>

  <section|What this closes and what it does
  not><label|what-this-closes-and-what-it-does-not>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Closes: the third clause of <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-scribe-clock-inputs>
    (F4 of #357), given the chart receipt <verbatim|1 \<less\>= b_i \<less\>=
    tiltcap(j_i)> (which the selected chart supplies for every <verbatim|i>,
    as above); and the tilt-cap zero-rate ticket in
    <verbatim|trace-small-means.tex>.

    <item>Not addressed: the two ratio limits in
    <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-scribe-clock-inputs> (<verbatim|zeta(j)/hatBeta_j
    -\<gtr\> 1>, source <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.gamut>;
    <verbatim|zeta(j)/zeta(summit j) -\<gtr\> 1>, source
    <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Barry>, uses <verbatim|PostT>); the summit
    ticket <verbatim|hatBeta_{summit(j)} \<less\>= 2 hatBeta_j>
    (<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.bond>, <verbatim|stickK>, uses
    <verbatim|PostT> and <verbatim|back_gate>). These remain inputs.

    <item>The manuscript's chart receipt is stated in
    <verbatim|trace-mission-price.tex> (l. 63\U67) and
    <verbatim|trace-small-means.tex> (l. 44\U46) as part of the selected
    chart receipt; this section derives it from the exponent window of the
    gallery's chart output, whose own producer (the three-panel chart result,
    F2 of #357) is still conditional.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Open questions><label|open-questions>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>None identified for the two lemmas. The identification "permitted
    angular bound = <verbatim|log log hatBeta_{j}>" is source-read
    (<verbatim|TimberSky.high>), not stated elsewhere in the manuscript; a
    reviewer should confirm that the gallery's "angular bound" is meant to be
    this quantity.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Recorded in the PR body (checker, unit tests, full <verbatim|existence.tex>
  build, page inspection). No Lean command was run: the Mathlib dependencies
  cannot be fetched in this sandbox (see earlier runs); the correspondence
  above is textual.

